  "notes": [
    "All real-image recognition variants bypass the Indra detector and orientation model. E-selected row boxes are frozen from saved recognition_rows inside E-selected vertical bands.",
    "No E recognized text is used as output fallback; GT is used only to score real-image variants.",
    "E original/inverted frame evaluations repeat 3 times and predictions agree. Other initial ablations run once; the white-core+CJK candidate has a separate 3-repeat confirmation.",
    "Annotated controls use exactly 32 subtitle frames / 85 annotated lines / 925 characters. These ideal coordinates are diagnostic, not a deployable detector.",
    "Rendered controls reuse the same private text, Hiragino Gothic W3 42px, and known glyph rectangles; black/white controls are polarity counterparts. The two outlined controls share glyphs/boxes and differ only in background.",
    "The textured rendered background is a 16x16 downsample then enlargement of the same source frame. This is a controlled synthetic diagnostic, not measured real-video accuracy.",
    "White-core uses the existing OcrBitmapInputs RGB threshold: min channel >=210 and max-min <=45 -> black, else white. No threshold was tuned for this experiment.",
    "CJK means direct use of the bundled CJK recognizer through recognize(vertical=True); no actual image rotation occurs. This bypasses automatic script routing.",
    "The pinned model has no mask.onnx and rec_window=3. The no-mask variants are redundant no-op controls and do not establish an effect of CenterMask.",
    "This is exploratory investigation on already-seen data, not independent validation. No best mode is selected per image and no device/latency claim is made.",
    "App source and normal E behavior are unchanged. No images, GT, predictions, frame IDs or local paths are included in this summary."
  ],
